PALIMPSEST_TURN {"text":"## State found\n\nThe migration was already present as the canonical commit `453aa7f` (`Migrate site readings service to gRPC`), with a clean working tree. The project DB still held a stale formal attempt (`grpc-contract`) whose execution world was based on the same commit — so it had no delta and could not honestly be completed.\n\nI reviewed the actual implementation and tests rather than relying on the commit message:\n\n- `proto/energy.proto` — `energy.v1.EnergyService` with unary `GetReading` and server-streaming `StreamReadings`; stable field numbers and `optional int32 limit`.\n- `service/wire.js` — built-ins-only protobuf codec and 5-byte gRPC framing.\n- `service/grpc_server.js` — HTTP/2 server with gRPC content type, frames, trailers, and the documented status mapping.\n- `service/grpc_client.js` — real streaming client returning the same shapes/messages as REST.\n- `test/server.test.js` / `test/integration.test.js` — protocol and live client/server tests, including REST-vs-gRPC comparisons.\n- `test/rest.test.js` — unchanged from the REST baseline.\n\n## Verification actually run\n\n```\nnode --test --test-isolation=none\n```\n\nResult: **26 tests, 26 pass, 0 fail** (~324 ms). This includes real HTTP/2 calls, streaming order/limit semantics, unknown-site `NOT_FOUND`/`unknown_site`, invalid-limit handling, exact epoch-ms `atMs`, one sub-16KiB frame per reading, malformed/oversized requests, and concurrency.\n\nThe literal `node --test` was also attempted; it fails in this sandbox with `spawn EPERM` because the runner cannot spawn isolated worker processes. That is the fallback case documented in `README.md`, not a product failure — the same suite was run in-process instead.\n\n## Project state recorded\n\n- Journal entry `pje-01f0c8dba60a21162169aed9b841bf03` records the verification evidence.\n- The stale attempt was closed as a **successor**, and the redundant task graph was retired by typed plan revision **revision 1** (`grpc-contract`, `grpc-service`, `verify-migration` → stale; attempt → cancelled).\n- Episode conclusion **DELIVER** recorded (`episode-ac4823af7e9d9fdbb21c2946`), with all 12 deliverable artifacts confirmed present, tracked, and committed at `453aa7f`.\n- No open tasks or attempts remain; `session.mayEnd` is true.\n\nNo code changes were required in this session: fabricating a new delta for an already-committed migration would have been settlement theater. The migration is ready for operator review/promotion; the recorded conclusion is my judgement, not operator acceptance.","toolCalls":["tool/call:palimpsest_continuity","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:pwsh","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","too